From bb17ff6cab877df6e4619793eb10904a5e07a638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:24:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Views: points, block accessor, context, workspace header,
 lifetime

- getPoints: view on a range of points of a view, the counterpart of
  getComponents, to process a range with the functions which process all
  the points of a view (rotations, evaluate, field operations).
- isUniform is false for an empty view, as documented.
- FieldView is checked to be trivially copyable; its use in device code
  is documented.
- getTangentOperatorBlockView on a material data view.
- updateValues on state views with an execution context.
- extractInternalStateVariable from a material state manager with field
  operations (device arrays).
- BehaviourIntegrationWorkSpace in its own header, included by
  Integrate.hxx: the functions on views no longer require the header of
  the material data managers.
- the views and the workspace can't be built for a temporary behaviour;
  the lifetime of the behaviour and the copies of the views are
  documented; the outputs of a view must not overlap each other.
